  <revision rev="7" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>b59edc2fd1295e1e46b46cfd1fd72631</srcmd5>
    <version>1.5.4</version>
    <time>1786543936</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update to 1.5.4

Upstream point release; no runtime or build dependency floors changed.

Two packaging fixes came out of the rebuild. Eight test deselects are dropped
because upstream's pydantic compatibility fix in load/serializable.py makes
the repr and serialization snapshot tests pass against the pydantic currently
in Factory -- proven with an A/B build rather than assumed, taking the
deselect list from 20 to 12. The comment on the three remaining test_graph.py
deselects was also wrong: they fail for a missing grandalf, not for pydantic.

Please note this is a lockstep pair with python-langchain-anthropic 1.5.5,
submitted alongside it: that release raises its floor to langchain-core
&gt;= 1.5.4, so anthropic is unresolvable until this lands.

Verified on aarch64: build green for python313 and python314, rpmlint
0 errors / 0 warnings / 0 badness.</comment>
    <requestid>1370780</requestid>
  </revision>
